   "desc": "Chicago AI, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup Join us on Dec 8 for the “How to Let Long-tail Guide Your 3D Annotation” workshop with [Eric Hofesmann](https://www.linkedin.com/in/eric-hofesmann/). **Date, Time and Location** Dec 08, 2026 9:00 AM - 10:00 AM PST Online. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/how-to-let-long-tail-guide-your-3d-annotation-december-8-2026)** Autonomous driving models rarely fail on the common case. They fail on the long-tail: the pedestrian stepping out from behind a parked truck or a construction zone that matches nothing in the training set. Each of those moments lives in synchronized multi-sensor data, made up of a LiDAR sweep, a ring of cameras, a timestamp, and a calibration. Fixing one means finding it, labeling it in 3D, and proving the next model handles it. In this live session, we will take long-tail driving scenarios from discovery to 3D labels to evaluation, and make the case that 3D ground truth should be built where your data lives, not exported away from it.",
